Article 1 Definitions
------------------------------------------------------------------------

1.1 "The Software"
    means the source code, binary files, documentation,
    configuration files, resource files, sample code,
    test cases, and any part or derivative work thereof
    attached to this license.

1.1.1 Scope Exclusion (Upstream and GPL-Covered Parts)
      This license applies **only** to the parts of the
      project authored by the Parlz copyright holder
      (in this repository: `userland/`, `scripts/`, `web/`,
      the distribution-packaging layer, and the
      documentation), and only to the extent the copyright
      holder is entitled to license them.

      It does **not** apply to, and does not attempt to
      relicense:
      (a) the Linux kernel tree (`linux-7.2.5/`), including
          any file the Parlz project added to or modified
          inside that tree, which remains licensed under
          the GNU General Public License version 2 only
          (GPL-2.0-only);
      (b) third-party components distributed with the
          project (for example BusyBox, SYSLINUX, bash,
          nano, wget, glibc, libxcrypt, OpenSSL, curl,
          miniz, GCC, LLVM), which remain under their own
          upstream licenses;
      (c) any other code bearing its own license header or
          SPDX identifier, in which case that header
          prevails over this license.

      Where this license and the license of an upstream
      component conflict, the upstream license governs that
      component. The authoritative component-by-component
      breakdown is the `LICENSE` file at the repository root
      and `/usr/share/licenses/README` inside the delivered
      images.

1.2 "Derivative Work"
    means any work based on all or part of the Software,
    created through modification, translation, adaptation,
    reorganization, extension, deletion, merging, linking,
    or any other means. This includes traditional software
    derivative works and model derivative works (see 1.7).

1.3 "Distribute"
    means to provide the Software or its Derivative Work
    to any third party in any form, including copying,
    transmission, uploading, downloading, public release,
    sharing, mirroring, packaging, integrated release,
    or providing through network services or APIs.

1.4 "Contribution"
    means any code, documentation, translation, design,
    suggestion, issue report, test case, patch, or any
    other content you submit to the Software.

1.5 "You"
    means any individual or legal entity exercising
    rights granted by this license.

1.6 "Copyright Holder"
    means the original author and any subsequent
    copyright owner of the Software.

1.7 "Model Derivative Work"
    means any model, weight, parameter, embedding, or
    generative system arising from any of the following:
    (a) a model trained using the Software or a Derivative
        Work as a training framework, inference engine,
        data processing pipeline, or training data
        generation tool;
    (b) a model produced by fine-tuning, distillation,
        quantization, pruning, or merging of the Software
        or a Derivative Work, where the Software or
        Derivative Work itself is a model, weight, or
        inference code;
    (c) a model trained on synthetic data generated by
        the Software or a Derivative Work.
    Whether a Model Derivative Work triggers the open
    source obligation is set out in Article 3.7.

1.8 "Corresponding Source"
    means all source code required to generate, install,
    run, and modify the Software or a Derivative Work,
    including build scripts, configuration files,
    interface definitions, and the training code and
    data manifest used to train a Model Derivative Work.


