Article 3 Basic Obligations
------------------------------------------------------------------------

3.1 Include License
    When distributing the Software or Derivative Works,
    you must include the full text of this license.
    It may not be deleted, modified, or replaced.
    The license should be placed in a prominent
    location, such as a LICENSE file in the project
    root directory.

3.2 Retain Copyright Notice
    You must retain all copyright notices, author
    attributions, license notices, and rights notices
    in the Software. They may not be deleted or hidden.

3.3 Mark Modifications
    When distributing a modified version, you must
    clearly indicate:
    (a) what you modified;
    (b) the date of modification;
    (c) the identity of the modifier (optional).

3.4 Derivative Works Must Be Open Source
    Derivative Works must continue to use this license.
    They may not be relicensed under any other license,
    and may not be distributed in closed-source form.
    If a Derivative Work contains all or part of the
    Software, the whole must use this license and its
    source code must be made public.

3.5 No Implied Endorsement
    You may not imply that the Software or Derivative
    Works have any commercial cooperation, sponsorship,
    endorsement, or affiliation with the Copyright
    Holder, unless you have prior written permission.

3.6 Network Service Clause
    If you provide the Software or a Derivative Work
    as a network service to third parties, you must
    make the Corresponding Source available to all
    users of that service. This clause references
    GNU AGPL v3 Section 13.

3.7 Open Source Obligation for Model Derivative Works
    (a) If you distribute a Model Derivative Work, you
        must simultaneously make public:
        (i) the model weights or parameters;
        (ii) the training code used to produce the model;
        (iii) a manifest of training data sources and
              how they were obtained.
    (b) If a Model Derivative Work is used only internally
        and not distributed, no open source obligation
        is triggered.
    (c) If you use the Software only for inference and
        do not train or fine-tune, the outputs are not
        considered Model Derivative Works.
    (d) This clause does not require disclosure of your
        proprietary data or trade secrets unrelated to
        the Software, but you must disclose the data
        source manifest.

3.8 Upstream Contribution Clause
    (a) If you use a modified version of the Software or
        a Derivative Work for commercial distribution,
        you must submit your modifications to the core
        functionality of the Software to the original
        repository as patches, pull requests, or
        equivalent forms.
    (b) Such submission is not required to be merged,
        but must actually be submitted and publicly
        accessible.
    (c) If the original repository is closed or
        inaccessible, you may publish the patches in
        your own repository and note the source in the
        documentation.
    (d) This clause does not apply to modifications
        solely for configuration, interface, or
        localization.


