     continue under PARLZ or switch to GPLv3, without
     case-by-case legal judgment.

12.3.1 Not GPLv2-only
       The declaration in 12.3 concerns **GPLv3** only.
       GPLv2-only code (notably the Linux kernel covered by
       12.2.1) cannot be merged into, or relicensed under,
       this license: the GPLv2 does not permit upgrading to
       a different license without every copyright holder's
       consent. For the kernel, GPLv2-only terms apply
       unchanged, and this license neither grants nor
       removes any right in it.

